# Task 3 – Git Branching Strategies

## 1. GitFlow

```text
master
  │
develop
  ├── feature/*
  ├── release/*
  └── hotfix/*
```

### Use Case

**GitFlow** is commonly used when development follows structured or scheduled release cycles.

---

## 2. GitHub Flow

```text
main
  │
  └── feature
        │
        ▼
   Pull Request
        │
        ▼
       main
```

### Use Case

**GitHub Flow** is suitable for teams that want a simple workflow with frequent integration and continuous delivery.

---

## 3. Trunk-Based Development

```text
Developer A ─┐
Developer B ─┼──► main
Developer C ─┘
```

### Use Case

**Trunk-Based Development** focuses on frequent integration into a shared main/trunk branch and works well with strong CI/CD practices.

---

## My Choices

| Scenario                               | Preferred Strategy      |
| -------------------------------------- | ----------------------- |
| Startup shipping quickly               | GitHub Flow             |
| Large team with scheduled releases     | GitFlow                 |
| Frequent integration with strong CI/CD | Trunk-Based Development |

